# grav_tether addon - Weapons hold-click popup for the sbs_utils grav_tether primitive.
#
# The physics + impulse enforcement live in sbs_utils.procedural.grav_tether (the
# primitive auto-runs its own tick, so just loading this addon + calling attach is
# enough - no activation step). This file is only the UX: a Weapons HOLD-CLICK on an
# object raises a hold-menu whose action is chosen by the target's ROLE.
#
# Engine-verified: the hold-click popup shows and toggles tether state in real Cosmos.
#
# Role -> mode (confirmed roles; pickups carry item,upgrade):
#   item / upgrade                -> Reel (draw in for collection)
#   station / asteroid / __npc__  -> Tow  (rope rest-length 500, stiffness ~5)
#   anything else                 -> Lock (rigid grab)
#   already tethered              -> Release
#
# Impulse-only is canonical (old-game Arena a28): the primitive caps the source back to
# impulse by default (grav_tether_set_overspeed_default to change to snap/off).

# THE OBJECT UNDER THE CURSOR, NOT THE WEAPONS LOCK. `WEAPONS_POPUP_ID` is what the
# gunner actually held the button on; `WEAPONS_SELECTED_ID` is whatever the console
# happens to have targeted, which for a tether is the wrong object nearly every time -
# you tow the derelict while you are still locked on the raider shooting at you. Gated on
# the selection, this menu offered to tether the WEAPONS TARGET no matter what was
# clicked, and offered nothing at all when the console had no lock. It is 0 for a
# hold-click on empty space, so the guard is required, not defensive.
//popup/weapons if has_any_role(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__") and WEAPONS_POPUP_ID != 0 and WEAPONS_POPUP_ID != WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID
    # grav_tether_HAS (the registry), not grav_tether_get (the live engine connection).
    # A Tow is a rope-TOGGLE: it deletes the connection whenever the load is inside the
    # rope length and re-adds it when the load drifts out - so `get` reads None for most
    # of a perfectly normal tow. Gated on that, this menu offered "Grav Tow" to something
    # already under tow and never offered "Release", so a crew could not let go.
    gt_has = grav_tether_has(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    if gt_has:
        + "Release":
            grav_tether_release(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    if not gt_has and has_any_role(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, "item,upgrade"):
        + "Grav Reel":
            grav_tether_reel(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)
    if not gt_has and has_any_role(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, "station,asteroid,__npc__"):
        + "Grav Tow":
            grav_tether_tow(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, 500)
    if not gt_has and not has_any_role(WEAPONS_POPUP_ID, "item,upgrade,station,asteroid,__npc__"):
        + "Grav Lock":
            grav_tether_lock(WEAPONS_ORIGIN_ID, WEAPONS_POPUP_ID)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIGHTER: the nose is the cursor.
#
# A pilot gets one button (the cockpit console owns it; see hangar/hangar.mast). It
# nose-aims, and when the target says what to do it just does it - a rock is an anchor, a
# pod is a pickup, and making a pilot confirm that is a menu for the sake of a menu. When
# the target is genuinely a CHOICE the button synthesizes this popup on it instead.
#
# Path B: the event is fabricated, not clicked, so this consumes NO select channel -
# comms, weapons and science selects all stay free. Capital ships reach the same actions
# through //popup/weapons above; this is the same verbs, a different way in.

//popup/tether if has_any_role(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__,cockpit")
    lmtf_towed = grav_tether_involves(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
    << "Grav-tether: {lm_tether_target_name(TETHER_SELECTED_ID)}"

    if lmtf_towed:
        + "Release":
            grav_tether_release_any(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
            lm_tether_cycle_reset(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)

    if not lmtf_towed:
        + "Tow":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "tow")
        + "Lock":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "lock")
        + "Swing":
            lm_tether_apply(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, TETHER_SELECTED_ID, "swing")
        # Target correction from INSIDE the popup - still no select channel. Walks
        # outward through the cone and wraps, so it can never dead-end.
        + "Cycle target":
            lmtf_next = lm_tether_cycle_next(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID)
            if lmtf_next is not None:
                lm_tether_open_popup(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, lmtf_next.id)


# The beam breaks under hard fire, so towing under attack is a real risk rather than a
# free ride. //damage/object fires per hit and carries the amount in EVENT.sub_float;
# only a heavy hit shakes a tether loose, or every skirmish would drop every load.
//damage/object if grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID) or grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_ORIGIN_ID)
    # Declared in __init__.mast; defaulted again here so a shot arriving before this
    # addon's top level has run cannot NameError the route out of existence.
    default LM_TETHER_BREAK_DAMAGE = 15
    lmgt_hit = EVENT.sub_float or 0
    ->END if lmgt_hit < LM_TETHER_BREAK_DAMAGE
    if grav_tether_involves(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID):
        grav_tether_release_any(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID)
        comms_broadcast(DAMAGE_TARGET_ID, "Grav-tether shaken loose by the hit.")


# Ran the reserves dry mid-haul. The library drops the load rather than pinning the ship
# at zero energy - being slow is a mechanic, being stranded is not.
//shared/signal/grav_tether_dry
    default SOURCE_ID = 0
    ->END if SOURCE_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, "Grav-tether offline - not enough power to hold the load.")


# Too fast to get hold of. Says WHY, or the button just looks broken.
//shared/signal/grav_tether_too_fast
    default SOURCE_ID = 0
    ->END if SOURCE_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SOURCE_ID, "Target is under power - cripple its engines before you can get a lock.")


# A hulk cashed in at a friendly station. The tick does the work; this is the telling.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_salvage_delivered
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    default UNITS = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, f"Hulk delivered - {UNITS} units of salvage aboard.")


# --- phase 5 -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A black hole is the anchor the swing was invented for. Offered only when one is
# actually in reach, and the rope is clamped clear of the gravity well by
# lm_tether_swing_hole - the tether must never be the thing that drops someone in.
//popup/tether if has_any_role(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, "__player__,cockpit") and lm_tether_nearest_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID) is not None
    + "Slingshot the black hole":
        lm_tether_swing_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID, lm_tether_nearest_hole(TETHER_ORIGIN_ID))


# Pinned by a hostile beam. Says what to do about it, because a ship that is suddenly
# not going anywhere with no explanation reads as a bug.
//shared/signal/lm_tether_pinned
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Caught in a hostile grav-tether - burn hard away to tear loose.")

//shared/signal/lm_tether_broke_free
    default SHIP_ID = 0
    ->END if SHIP_ID == 0
    comms_broadcast(SHIP_ID, "Tether snapped - you are free.")
